 ('000f305f-99bf-563c-b513-cf8c3bb0b064', '2025-2026', 13503, 10427, 2169, 13.14, 65.15, 3.47, 99.9, '{"4.0": 22.76, "3.75-3.99": 16.94, "3.50-3.74": 13.9, "3.25-3.49": 12.65, "3.00-3.24": 8.96, "2.50-2.99": 15.14, "2.0-2.49": 8.68, "1.0-1.99": 0.92}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025): applicants, admits and enrollees are the sums of the men, women and unknown-sex rows (6,243+7,187+73 applied; 4,811+5,560+56 admitted; 1,056+1,087+26 enrolled). The residency table gives only enrollees: 2,004 in-state, 140 out-of-state, 25 international; applicants and admits by residency are blank, so intl_applicants/intl_admits are null. GPA distribution is the ''all enrolled students'' column (0.05% below 1.0 not shown). Undergrad enrollment is B1 ''Total All Undergraduates'' (11,691); intl_undergrads is B2 nonresident-alien total undergraduates (226; 215 degree-seeking). CDS C8F: ''The University of Akron is test optional.'' Class rank was reported by only 15.1% of first-years.', '46620fe5-5af2-56a1-83df-9bea0510833f');
