 ('000f305f-99bf-563c-b513-cf8c3bb0b064', '2026-2027', 11536, 19216, 19216, 2400, 13396, 1200, 1628, 200, 9112, false, true, 'CDS G1/G5 (full 2026-27 year, first-year): nonresident and international tuition $19,216 (in-state $11,536) plus $2,400 required fees; food and housing $13,396; books $1,200; transportation $2,000 (residents) is not included in other. CDS H6: institutional NON-need-based aid is available to nonresident aliens; 200 received it (avg $9,112, total $1,822,425; the form flags aid year 2023). The International Center''s own estimate (2025-26 rates) is $21,585 tuition and fees, $13,317 room and board, $1,328 health insurance, $2,559 books and personal expenses, total $38,789.; New international freshmen are automatically considered for merit scholarships with admission (based on GPA and curriculum, amounts vary; 12+ credits per semester, normally renewable for four years while in good standing at 2.0 GPA). The 2026-27 scholarship table does not state international-specific amounts. CDS H6: 200 nonresident undergraduates received institutional non-need aid, average $9,112.', '46620fe5-5af2-56a1-83df-9bea0510833f');
