 ('c3ea01d3-89ad-530b-9971-ebdf5a0728cb', '2025-2026', 24549, 17192, 2931, 348, 303, 223, 94, 6101, 4341, 18225, 12757, 548, 156, 5, 29, 10, 3.45, 99.93, '{"4.0": 5.7, "3.75-3.99": 21.1, "3.50-3.74": 23.25, "3.25-3.49": 20.96, "3.00-3.24": 18.3, "2.50-2.99": 10.58, "2.0-2.49": 0.07, "1.0-1.99": 0.03}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025): 24,549 applied, 17,192 admitted, 2,931 enrolled; residency by known address at application: in-state 6,101 applied / 4,341 admitted, out-of-state 18,225 / 12,757, international 223 applied / 94 admitted / 20 enrolled (international admit rate is well below the overall rate). Early decision: 348 applied, 303 admitted. The CDS lists 29% of enrolled first-years submitting SAT and 10% ACT; Coastal runs a test-optional program for freshmen with a 3.5 HS GPA. GPA distribution is the C11 ''all enrolled students'' column (sums to 99.99). The C9 score table is laid out unevenly in the PDF text; SAT section, SAT total and ACT composite percentiles were matched against the score-range distributions printed beside them. ACT subscore percentiles were not readable and are omitted. The C7 factor checkboxes are garbled (several rows show two marks), so factors are omitted.', '00251e54-2bf7-5f0c-9c9f-f12d692b32a2');
