 ('03788304-1a02-55e9-929c-46778bc8c026', '2025-2026', 13475, 10355, 1162, 408, 315, 10937, 8463, 2130, 1577, 43.22, 8.43, 3.24, 96.82, '{"4.0": 3.2, "3.75-3.99": 15.36, "3.50-3.74": 20.16, "3.25-3.49": 15.99, "3.00-3.24": 14.03, "2.50-2.99": 21.4, "2.0-2.49": 8.53, "1.0-1.99": 1.33}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025 first-year class). Residency split: in-state 10,937 applied / 8,463 admitted / 1,092 enrolled; out-of-state 2,130 / 1,577 / 51; international 408 / 315 / 19 (about 77% of international applicants admitted). Undergraduate enrollment 10,260 and nonresident undergraduates 217 are the B1/B2 ''Total Undergraduates'' figures; the 16:1 student-to-faculty ratio is CDS section I (College Navigator shows 17:1). No waiting list, early decision or early action. Test-optional in practice, so SAT/ACT percentiles describe the 43% (SAT) and 8% (ACT) of enrollees who submitted scores.', '35e79ea9-996f-558b-803d-aa74a6f77658');
