 ('cb7a90c7-d930-51aa-a6df-5f58830558c6', '2026-2027', 6099, 21655, 21655, 16414, 1288, 'merit_only', 287, 14494, false, true, 'CDS G1/G5/H6 (30 credits for the full year at $203.29 per credit in-state / $721.84 per credit out-of-state; per-credit rates equal the 2024-25 IPEDS rates, so these may be carried forward). Food and housing on campus $16,414 (housing $11,324 + food $5,090). H6: 287 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $14,494. The international admissions page estimates $17,324 tuition and fees for 24 credits (fall + spring) and a $46,246 total cost of attendance.; President''s International Scholarship: $6,000 per year, renewable up to four years, for F-1/J-1 freshmen with 3.5+ GPA (4.0 scale), SAT/ACT/CLT scores and proof of English proficiency; automatic consideration on admission, limited number. Florida Linkage Institute tuition waivers exist for specific countries. International students are not eligible for federal aid.', 'a9068e38-1935-5a3b-9c5e-82aeab84a0d8');
