 ('7590938f-4869-5fb6-b0c7-c4936a9b14db', '2025-2026', 2761, 2249, 938, 65, 46, 2410, 2024, 286, 179, 20.0, 1.4, 3.11, 93.18, '{"4.0": 7.44, "3.75-3.99": 11.33, "3.50-3.74": 11.9, "3.25-3.49": 13.27, "3.00-3.24": 12.93, "2.50-2.99": 25.63, "2.0-2.49": 16.25, "1.0-1.99": 1.26}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025 first-years, IU South Bend campus): 2,761 applied, 2,249 admitted, 938 enrolled; international 65 applied / 46 admitted (71%) / 5 enrolled, out-of-state 286 / 179 / 29. No waitlist. C9: 188 enrolled students submitted SAT (20.0%) and 13 submitted ACT (1.4%), so the ACT percentiles rest on very few students. GPA distribution is the ''all enrolled students'' column of C11 as printed (sums to 100.01). Undergraduate enrollment is B1 ''Total All Undergraduate Students'' (4,206); intl_undergrads is the B2 ''Nonresidents'' total undergraduates (69; 14 first-years). Student-faculty ratio 15 is the CDS I-section ratio (3,874.69 students / 264 faculty).', '89efea44-dc8c-5e62-8e42-5f8c28ad42f3');
