 ('f6040c2d-ba4d-59dc-aba6-4510dba616b5', '2026-2027', 24298, 14360, 3935, 42593, 'merit_only', false, true, false, 'Kent State''s estimated expenses for an international undergraduate (2026-27, used for I-20s): $24,298 tuition and fees combined for the year (out-of-state rate), $14,360 living expenses and $3,935 medical insurance plus books/supplies. International students must buy the university health plan unless they qualify for a waiver. The Kent CDS did not report 2026-27 tuition (G1 blank), so in-state tuition is left null.; Global Scholarship (automatic on admission, Kent campus, F-1, first-year or transfer) per year by US GPA: 3.70+ $12,000; 3.60-3.69 $10,000; 3.50-3.59 $7,000; 3.49 and below $4,300; Honors College admits $15,000 plus a $2,000 Honors scholarship. Renewable for 8 semesters with full-time enrollment. Kent says scholarships are partial and could total up to $68,000 over four years. CDS H6: 551 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $10,799 (the CDS checkboxes for need-based vs non-need-based are inconsistent).', '09b952a9-0e65-51c8-93c0-e7474aaefe72');
