 ('05de2d4c-d45d-5bd4-b748-d03cc469394c', '2026-2027', 7770, 18772, 18772, 1618, 13826, 1100, 'merit_only', false, 48, 23681, false, true, 'CDS G1 (first-year, 2026-27): in-state tuition $7,770, out-of-state/nonresident $18,772, required fees $1,618, food and housing $13,826. Tuition varies by program (G4: 86.5% pay more than the G1 figure). CDS H6: only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 48 nonresidents received it (average $23,681).; International students are treated as nonresidents for scholarships. The John Marshall Scholarship (freshman merit; high school GPA and, where applicable, test scores) pays nonresidents $14,000 (GPA 3.9+ with ACT 30/SAT 1360), $9,000 (GPA 3.8), $7,000 (GPA 3.5) or $5,000 (GPA 3.0) per year; it is renewable for four years. Only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents (CDS H6).', '9aa61030-599e-5e5f-b6a0-5c3cb9a79d89');
