 ('aa397d16-785c-5d69-8be9-3f8b94a04053', '2026-2027', 9668, 10668, 11668, 500, 1385, 'merit_only', false, true, false, true, 'Estimated costs page (based on 2025-26 actual costs, subject to change): annual tuition and fees $9,668 Louisiana, $10,668 out of state, $11,668 international (so the tuition figures here include required fees). Health insurance for international students only is $500 per year (shown as extra fees). On-campus housing and meal plan $9,500-$11,900; off-campus housing and food $12,572; transportation $3,754 and personal expenses $2,742 are not charged by the university.; International scholarship for first-time freshmen: $1,000 per year for a 3.0 high school GPA plus one of IELTS 6.5, TOEFL 79, Duolingo 110, PTE 56 or SAT 1200 (the page lists every row at $1,000; it does not say whether the awards stack). Renewable for up to 8 continuous fall/spring semesters; students must be fully admitted first; awards depend on funding and are not guaranteed; students sponsored by government or government-affiliated programs are not eligible. No scholarship deadline is printed. The page names no need-based aid for international students. Applicants indicate interest in scholarships on the admission application.', 'a0db5355-25b4-5b2a-932e-83ddb106ff84');
