 ('75fa337b-1b23-5aaf-b883-8ba802560f40', '2025-2026', 26224, 23443, 3816, 1459, 1220, 21206, 19137, 3559, 3086, 10, 3.35, 94.08, '{"4.0": 11.62, "3.75-3.99": 12.15, "3.50-3.74": 17.58, "3.25-3.49": 16.52, "3.00-3.24": 17.55, "2.50-2.99": 23.09, "2.0-2.49": 1.45, "1.0-1.99": 0.06}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025 entering class). Residency split is by known physical address at application: in-state 21,206 / out-of-state 3,559 / international 1,459 applicants; 19,137 / 3,086 / 1,220 admitted; 3,590 / 175 / 51 enrolled. Undergrad enrollment is B1 ''Total Undergraduate Students'' (8,091 men + 10,957 women = 19,048); the nonresident count (332) is the B2 ''Total Undergraduates'' column. SAT percentiles cover only the 10% (364) of enrollees who submitted SAT scores; no ACT scores were reported. The SAT Math 25th percentile is printed as 418 in the CDS. CDS C14 (domestic): closing date 3/1, priority 12/1; early action closes 12/1.', '876e598b-c1c6-5c63-8d12-62a7deb196f1');
