 ('cd94d931-611a-5f28-9d12-e2c1d4d1806d', '2025-2026', 5226, 4479, 803, 253, 150, 4653, 4075, 320, 254, 3, 90, 3.52, 91.41, '{"4.0": 17.03, "3.75-3.99": 30.11, "3.50-3.74": 15.53, "3.25-3.49": 10.63, "3.00-3.24": 11.04, "2.50-2.99": 10.63, "2.0-2.49": 4.22, "1.0-1.99": 0.68}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025 entering class). International applicants were admitted at a much lower rate (150 of 253, 59%) than in-state (87.6%) or out-of-state (79.4%) applicants; international enrollees: 28. Only 28 students submitted SAT scores (3%) and 723 submitted ACT (90%), so SAT percentiles rest on a very small sample. No early decision or early action, no waitlist. Undergrad count and intl_undergrads are the B1 totals (4,056 undergraduates, 240 nonresidents). The posted PDF looks like a working copy (placeholder text in the respondent block and 2024-2025 page headers) although its items are for fall 2025.', 'cb433b1d-a768-5948-8683-f4bbb6866bc0');
