 ('PTE', 46, 'PTE Academic.'),
 ('CAMBRIDGE', 169, 'Cambridge English Language Assessment score of 169+.')) v;
insert into cost_aid (institution_id, year, tuition_intl_usd, required_fees_usd, room_board_usd, books_usd, total_coa_usd, intl_aid_policy, meets_full_need, merit_scholarships, notes, source_id) values
 ('f13570fc-7449-57eb-8ffc-e1b7e1e94158', '2026-2027', 29572, 1841, 12928, 1200, 45541, 'merit_only', false, true, 'UNR international undergraduate cost table (the page does not state an academic year; used as the current estimate): base tuition $9,383 ($312.75/credit, 30 credits) plus non-resident tuition fee $20,189 (tuition_intl 29,572), mandatory student fees $1,841 (incl. international student fees). On-campus housing $7,000-$11,000 and meals $5,928-$7,488; room_board and total use the low end (published total range $45,541-$51,101). The CDS 2025-26 G1 lists nonresident tuition $28,308 plus fees $1,642. Health insurance and personal costs are not in the total. A separate admissions page still says $23,562 a year in estimated tuition, which conflicts with the cost table.; The international admissions page says new international students can receive $1,000 to $12,000 scholarships, and general University scholarships range from $500 to $8,000 per year. OISS awards $300-$5,000 per year to degree-seeking F-1/J-1 students. Need-based help for international students is limited to the Institutional Methodology form after one year of study (priority Feb. 1). A Pack Exchange Program (200% of base tuition) exists only for international students who graduated from a U.S. high school in listed western states. CDS H6 (2025-26): 1,484 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $2,862. No conditional-admission or intensive-English pathway is described on the pages checked.', '6aef21b6-3d5f-5ccd-b7fc-c722224c7b0e');
