 ('24252c63-25f4-5004-8fa0-5a633fd0a1e5', '2024-2025', 9296, 23490, 23490, 2714, 15230, 1200, 'merit_only', true, 6037, false, true, 'CDS G1 (first-year, 2024-25; the 2023-24 CDS reports the following year''s prices). UNC''s tuition page for 2026-27 lists nonresident tuition of $13,047 per semester at 15 credits, plus per-credit fees (activity $72.58, capital $59.30 and LEAF $1.00, each capped at 10 credits; technology $15.23) and a one-time $260 new-student fee; it gives no housing figure. CDS H6: 49 degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid in 2023-24 (average $6,037, total $295,797).; Automatic first-year scholarships listed for non-resident and international students for fall 2026/spring 2027 entry, by weighted GPA: Trustee $7,500 per year (4.00), Presidential $6,500 (3.80-3.99), Provost $5,000 (3.40-3.79), Bear $4,000 (3.00-3.39). Fall 2027 amounts were not yet published. 49 nonresidents received institutional aid in 2023-24 (CDS H6, average $6,037); the page names no international-only or need-based award.', '50c8b6d1-0e87-5381-9e86-6fa477aea6eb');
