 ('aa657be8-4ecf-5b66-b69d-81f91cc59e1c', '2025-2026', 5442, 5068, 1549, 328, 298, 3886, 3669, 1228, 1101, 2, 44, 3.61, 98.8, '{"4.0": 16.5, "3.75-3.99": 29.0, "3.50-3.74": 21.0, "3.25-3.49": 13.8, "3.00-3.24": 10.7, "2.50-2.99": 8.0, "2.0-2.49": 1.0, "1.0-1.99": 0.0}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (Fall 2025): men 1,997 + women 3,445 applied; residency rows sum to the totals (in-state 3,886 + out-of-state 1,228 + international 328 = 5,442). International: 328 applied, 298 admitted, 14 enrolled. No early decision or early action; no waitlist; deferral up to 1 year. Only 24 students (2%) reported SAT scores in C9, so SAT percentiles rest on a very small group; 680 (44%) reported ACT. GPA distribution is the ''all enrolled'' column of C11. Undergraduate enrollment and nonresident count are the B1/B2 ''Total Undergraduates'' figures (7,800; 167 nonresident).', 'fe126f61-482e-5663-bb93-0db90aa9d6e8');
