 ('recommendations', 'not_considered'),
 ('alumni_relation', 'considered')) v;
insert into test_policies (institution_id, cycle, policy, notes, source_id) values
 ('80e21a51-1e05-5d4a-ab42-e214dfd62d08', '2026-27', 'blind', 'SVSU does not use SAT/ACT for admission or most scholarships (the freshmen page calls this ''test-optional''; the CDS calls it test-blind). Scores are used only for English and math placement; without them students take SVSU placement testing or start in remedial courses. International applicants may also use SAT EBRW 500 or ACT 18 as proof of English.', 'a538154d-d83b-5236-9236-9dcbf6d17c71');
insert into application_requirements (institution_id, cycle, platforms, app_fee_usd, notes, source_id) values
 ('80e21a51-1e05-5d4a-ab42-e214dfd62d08', '2026-27', array['own']::text[], 50, 'Own online application. International first-year applicants pay a $50 application fee (domestic applicants pay none). Need a 2.5 GPA on a 4.0 scale (SVSU converts it; below 2.5 may be admitted on probation), a passport copy and a high school transcript (unofficial accepted for the decision, official on arrival). No essay or recommendation required (CDS C7). Direct admission to Nursing and Occupational Therapy exists for domestic freshmen on the admissions page.', '9ce08d9e-8409-5bd3-9ac0-8269e2506509');
insert into deadlines (id, institution_id, cycle, kind, plan_key, label, due_date, notes, source_id) values
 ('bfa9a31c-a3f6-50e7-8cf0-d3f85e760e7c', '80e21a51-1e05-5d4a-ab42-e214dfd62d08', '2026-27', 'application', 'ROLLING', 'International first-year application deadline, fall 2027', '2027-07-01', 'The page prints ''July 1'' for Fall (Nov 1 for Winter) with no year; taken as fall 2027. International first-years cannot start in Spring or Summer. SVSU admits on a rolling basis with no application closing date in the CDS.', '9ce08d9e-8409-5bd3-9ac0-8269e2506509');
insert into english_policies (institution_id, policy, waiver_notes, source_id) values
 ('80e21a51-1e05-5d4a-ab42-e214dfd62d08', 'required_nonnative', 'The page says the English requirement ''may be waived for applicants from certain countries'' without printing the list. Alternatives to a language test: SAT EBRW 500 or ACT English/writing 18. No conditional admission or ESL pathway is described on the international pages read.', '752022a4-30b2-5e5d-aabd-b71568efd34f');
insert into english_requirements (institution_id, status, source_id, test_key, min_total, notes)
