 ('dd3198d3-b17b-5afc-a85b-e1f48c3c70f4', '2025-2026', 6320, 4707, 1550, 228, 81, 5162, 3930, 930, 696, 12, 3.58, 96.38, '{"4.0": 21, "3.75-3.99": 22, "3.50-3.74": 20, "3.25-3.49": 16, "3.00-3.24": 12, "2.50-2.99": 9}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1: international first-year applicants 228, admitted 81 (36%), enrolled 6, far below the 74% overall admit rate, so SRU is not an automatic admit for international applicants; the CDS does not say why (for example incomplete applications). C2 says no waitlist policy, while SRU''s admissions page describes a waitlist for applicants below the guidelines. 12% (178 students) of enrolled first-years submitted SAT; the CDS prints ACT as 0% with 30 students, so pct_submit_act is left null. SAT/ACT percentiles are for those submitters only (ACT: 30 students). C7 marks test scores ''important'' although applications are test-optional. GPA distribution is the all-enrolled column of C11 (3.58 average). Undergraduate enrollment 7,088 and 248 nonresident undergraduates are CDS B1/B2 (fall 2025).', 'e2746f86-8786-582e-8c0c-b6c2495218b8');
