 ('9cec1fe5-c450-59be-b15e-0dbb28fca6cd', '2026-2027', 9036, 21820, 21820, 1830, 475, 11650, 810, 3655, 40240, 'merit_only', false, 81, 5225, false, 'USI international page, 2026-2027: tuition $21,820 (30 credits), university fees $1,830 plus a $475 first-semester-only fee, on-campus housing $5,778 and meal plan $5,872, textbooks $810, mandatory health insurance $1,655 and personal $2,000 (other = 3,655). Excludes travel, the $40 application fee, $50 housing application and $300 housing prepayment. Proof of funds: signed Statement of Finances and a bank statement of 3 months'' transactions, +$3,000 per dependent; no total amount is published.; CDS G1 (first-year): in-state tuition $9,035.70, fees $1,755, food and housing $11,644 (a second column prints fees of $1,240). H6: only institutional NON-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 81 nonresident undergraduates received it (avg $5,225).; CDS H6: only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 81 nonresident undergraduates received it (avg $5,225). USI''s international tuition page lists no international scholarships and the nonresident application asks for an award application, 2 recommendation letters and 2 essays (CDS H7). The David L. Rice merit scholarship targets Indiana and nearby Kentucky/Illinois residents.', '3bb12690-3ee5-5991-84be-70677ecb6d37');
