 ('2e1cf252-2d9e-5cf2-824d-6f6c42fbc5c4', '2024-2025', 8469, 8499, 7634, 1318, 8746, 26197, false, '2026-27 tuition page: undergraduate tuition $252 per credit hour resident and $582 nonresident ($252 + $330), plus mandatory fees of $29.20 per credit hour and an academic enhancement fee of $15 per hour. Catalog: international students are treated as nonresidents; fees include a $100 international maintenance fee per semester and mandatory health insurance. The Costs and Aid page (undated, accessed 2026-10-26) shows undergraduate annual estimates of $9,131 resident, $16,241 nonresident and $26,608 international, without saying what they include; these do not show the In-State Plus $1 rate. Confirm with SWOSU before relying on either figure.; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $8,469, out-of-state $8,499; on-campus food and housing $7,634, other $8,746; total_coa_usd is the out-of-state on-campus total. International students are classed as nonresidents; see the cycle notes for SWOSU''s published international cost estimate.; Federal aid is not available to international students. The 2025-26 catalog says SWOSU offers its In-State Plus $1 Program to international students (nonresidents paying in-state tuition plus $1 per credit hour, per SWOSU program materials); the exact rate and whether it is automatic could not be confirmed because SWOSU''s program page could not be loaded. Institutional scholarship eligibility for international students is not stated.', 'f6f0c92d-192e-5c87-8612-39f84c6f7cd3');
