 ('3c83d810-cf89-564b-ac78-5efc9448b2a1', '2025-2026', 3745, 3554, 543, 39, 39, 3579, 3389, 127, 126, 7, 1, 95, '{"4.0": 0.8, "3.75-3.99": 7.9, "3.50-3.74": 13.4, "3.25-3.49": 17.1, "3.00-3.24": 17.4, "2.50-2.99": 22.5, "2.0-2.49": 15.5, "1.0-1.99": 5.2}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2025 first-time, first-year): 3,745 applied, 3,554 admitted, 543 enrolled; the residency table lists 39 international applicants, all 39 admitted, 9 enrolled. Out-of-state counts exclude international. SAT scores were submitted by 7% (38 students) and ACT by 1% (6), so the SAT range rests on few students; no ACT percentiles were printed. C11 also shows 0.2% of students below a 1.0 GPA (not in the distribution). The average high school GPA in C12 is printed as ''85.7 or 3'' (a 100-point figure and a truncated 4.0 value), so gpa_avg is omitted.The CDS does not check the C6 open-admission boxes. Undergraduate enrollment 3,459 (IPEDS fall 2024) and 52 nonresident-alien undergraduates (IPEDS fall 2024 enrollment by race via the Urban Institute Education Data Portal).', '8810a589-4d17-5f7d-9d43-f1ca3a3e1c81');
