 ('ede00be9-8149-5aaa-9c78-6a86d28336bf', '2024-2025', 9748, 20794, 12748, 1296, 3514, 'merit_only', false, 91, 13584, false, true, 'IPEDS College Navigator 2024-25 first-time undergraduate expenses: tuition amounts include required fees; the out-of-state rate is the one that applies to international students (the university lists no separate international rate). The CDS left section G (2026-27 costs) blank. CDS H6: institutional aid for nonresidents is non-need-based only; 91 nonresident undergraduates received it (avg $13,584, total $1,236,168).; International incoming freshman scholarships are $1,000 to $4,000 a year for up to four years, by high school GPA (U.S. 4.0 scale) and English score: President''s International Excellence Award $3,001-$4,000 (GPA 3.5+, IELTS 7.0 or TOEFL iBT 94); International Achieve Scholar $2,001-$3,000 (3.3+, IELTS 6.5 / iBT 89); International Islander Scholar $1,001-$2,000 (3.2+, IELTS 6.5 / iBT 84); International Impact Scholar $1,000 (3.0+, IELTS 6.5 / iBT 79). Apply Oct. 15 to May 1. The scholarship page says these awards do not qualify the student for the in-state tuition waiver, and ESLI graduates are not eligible. No need-based institutional aid for nonresidents (CDS H6).', 'ab5caa81-1473-571a-8e0e-f13123dc81a8');
