 ('e2959ff6-ac6b-572f-9502-8ea8b5dd8b9a', '2025-2026', 5997, 18297, 18297, 4183, 11676, 1560, false, 'CDS G1 (first-year, 2025-26; no 2026-27 figures are posted): in-state tuition $5,997, out-of-state/nonresident $18,297, required fees $4,183, food and housing $11,676. CDS H6 lists 479 nonresident undergraduates with institutional aid (average $5,926), but the checked H6 box is unreadable and that page is headed 2023-2024, so the aid fields are left null.; The President''s Guaranteed Scholarship (first-time freshmen in the top half of their high school class) pays $500 to $4,000 a year depending on rank and test scores, renewable up to 4 years; only students in the top 25% may qualify for an out-of-state tuition waiver. The page does not say whether international students are eligible, and no international-specific scholarship is published, so aid policy is left unset.', '8cfd09f7-7ba1-563e-bb3e-7bc647c24720');
