 ('e23f16a9-8a9a-5efc-82f6-1c1e61dad791', '2025-2026', 8804, 7451, 457, 84, 81, 1800, 1465, 6920, 5905, 30, 67, 3.35, 97.2, '{"4.0": 12.6, "3.75-3.99": 11.5, "3.50-3.74": 15.3, "3.25-3.49": 17.3, "3.00-3.24": 18.5, "2.50-2.99": 21.2, "2.0-2.49": 2.9, "1.0-1.99": 0.7}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 for fall 2025 (the TSU 2025-26 CDS files are headed ''Common Data Set 2024-2025'' but ask for Fall 2025 data): 8,804 applied, 7,451 admitted (85%), 457 enrolled. International: 84 applied, 81 admitted (96%), 4 enrolled. GPA distribution is the ''all enrolled students'' column of C11. pct_submit_sat/act are the C9 percentages (138 SAT, 307 ACT of the 457 enrolled). C7 factors: academic GPA and test scores very important, rigor and class rank considered, everything else not considered (the x marks were readable). Undergraduate enrollment 4,221 and 74 nonresident undergraduates are from B1/B2 (fall 2025); student-to-faculty ratio 11 to 1 is CDS I-2 (College Navigator shows 13 to 1).', '4caaae2d-ff3c-5afd-94cb-f5abce8bf231');
