 ('ad96250b-5f00-5d5b-b637-19b8c6ef56f3', '2025-2026', 20772, 16735, 2908, 15452, 12418, 4880, 3914, 20, 1, 3.81, 100, '{"4.0": 34.56, "3.75-3.99": 17.92, "3.50-3.74": 19.36, "3.25-3.49": 16.88, "3.00-3.24": 9.49, "2.50-2.99": 1.69, "2.0-2.49": 0.1}'::jsonb, 'Fall 2025 first-time first-year cohort. Totals are the sum of the male + female + unknown-sex rows in CDS C1 (no single total is printed). The C1 residency table prints only in-state and out-of-state (together 20,332 applied and 16,332 admitted), so intl_applicants/intl_admits are left null; CDS B2 lists 15 nonresident first-year enrollees. TU says it is permanently test-optional; only 20% of enrollees submitted SAT (583 students) and 1% ACT (17), so the ACT percentiles rest on very few students. Average GPA 3.81 is weighted. Non-binding early action (C22): 15,387 applications, 12,668 admitted. No early decision, no waitlist.', 'ba9b733d-e873-5fe8-844d-7289588effbe');
