 ('43870941-5645-5abb-a696-bdbbca1f7b7a', '2024-2025', 9987, 19827, 9728, 1250, 3918, 34723, 'need_aware_limited', true, false, 'College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $9,987, out-of-state $19,827; on-campus food and housing $9,728, other expenses $3,918. total_coa_usd is the published out-of-state on-campus total (the rate an international student would normally face; UTRGV does not publish a separate international tuition rate on the pages read).; No automatic international merit scholarship amounts were found. International Student Services lists a $1,000 summer need-based grant for continuing students, the state-run Good Neighbor Scholarship (tuition exemption for students from Western Hemisphere countries other than Cuba and the U.S., selected by the Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board), and ''I am a Buddy'' awards of $500-$700 per semester for enrolled students. UTRGV''s I-20 estimate for a full-time overseas undergraduate paying non-resident tuition is $41,668 living independently (2026-27 table).', '2a5fef39-6d36-594f-9b6e-2b73b70e7e48');
