 ('490cfaec-cd3c-550a-ad1b-b32e8b9dee6a', '2025-2026', 21428, 14119, 1640, 118, 10394, 9118, 9394, 4883, 7.23, 23.07, 3.45, 100, '{"4.0": 5.85, "3.75-3.99": 25.31, "3.50-3.74": 21.21, "3.25-3.49": 17.17, "3.00-3.24": 15.05, "2.50-2.99": 13.77, "2.0-2.49": 1.64, "1.0-1.99": 0.0}'::jsonb, 'Fall 2025 entering class. International first-year applicants 1,640, admitted only 118 (7%), enrolled 56 (C1 residency table), so WCU admits far fewer internationals than domestic applicants. Enrolled is left null: C1 reports 2,936 enrolled (residency table; men 1,272 + women 1,679) but the full-time/part-time split (1,895) and the C9 test-submission counts imply a class near 1,900. WCU says it receives 9-10 applications per fall first-year space. Undergraduate total 10,268 and nonresident-alien undergraduates 223 are from CDS B1/B2.', '9ff119e2-ada7-5e06-8855-429ecd5222e3');
