 ('7e3e1d53-3af2-5072-94b1-18ac2faff41a', '2026-2027', 43836, 450, 200, 12099, 'need_aware_limited', true, true, false, 'Traditional undergraduate: tuition $21,918 per semester; required fees $225 per term (health & wellness $100, student activity $100, technology $25); international student fee $100 per term; standard residence hall $3,592 + standard meal plan $2,302 + NC meal plan tax $155.39 per term (annual room and board rounded). Program fees (e.g. nursing, labs) are extra.; Admitted international students are awarded a merit scholarship; the page says these ''can range from $15,000 - $30,500'' but are not guaranteed, and there are no full-ride awards. Additional aid is available through the Alternative Financial Aid Application (amounts not published). Most students must show $30,000-$49,000 in funds for the I-20, depending on scholarship.', '1e2ca5d9-3d56-529e-b52b-1e6997862034');
